hows-total-time-limit-exceeds-60s-judging-canceled","content":"Judge shows \"Total time limit exceeds 60s, judging canceled\""},"240":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-24","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-add-line-animation-effects-in-background","content":"How to add line animation effects in background?"},"241":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-25","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-much-does-hydro-cost","content":"How much does Hydro cost?"},"242":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-26","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#execve-no-such-file-or-directory","content":"execve: no such file or directory"},"243":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-27","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-customize-user-badges","content":"How to customize user badges?"},"244":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-28","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#why-cant-i-batch-download-multiple-files","content":"Why can't I batch download multiple files?"},"245":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-29","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#why-is-there-no-language-option-on-my-submission-page","content":"Why is there no language option on my submission page?"},"246":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-30","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#the-yarn-global-commands-have-been-remove-in-2x---consider-using-yarn-dlx-or-a-third-party-plugin-instead","content":"The 'yarn global' commands have been remove in 2.x - consider using 'yarn dlx' or a third-party plugin instead"},"247":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-31","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#im-in-a-computer-lab-environment-many-users-share-one-ip-and-trigger-rate-limits-how-to-solve","content":"I'm in a computer lab environment; many users share one IP and trigger rate limits. How to solve?"},"248":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-32","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#adjust-temporary-directory-size","content":"Adjust temporary directory size"},"249":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-33","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-can-i-quickly-get-familiar-with-system-features","content":"Refer to this post: https://hydro.ac/discuss/6172ceeed850d38c79ae18f9 for a serverless quick experience of system features.If you do not need heavy secondary development, we recommend using the online service directly. Problemsets with over 20,000 problems can be copied directly, with no need to buy cloud servers or maintain them manually.If you need customizations such as binding your own domain or changing logos, you can also enable advanced features in the admin panel yourself."},"250":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-34","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-can-i-quickly-get-familiar-with-system-features","content":"Users in the system only support edit and disable, not delete. This is to fundamentally prevent \"teaching accidents.\" Please do not request user deletion features. If you are certain you will never misoperate, develop that feature yourself."},"251":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-35","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-an-oj","content":"The judging system you are using now is just a program, not artificial intelligence. So in many places, you need to adapt to it. Otherwise, even if your answer is essentially correct, format errors can make the system unable to understand it and still result in wrong answers.The system workflow is as follows:"},"252":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-36","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-an-oj","content":"Teachers add problems in the system and strictly define input/output formats."},"253":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-37","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-an-oj","content":"Teachers add multiple sets of test data according to the problem format; each set includes input and expected output."},"254":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-38","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-an-oj","content":"Students read the problem and submit programs based on their understanding."},"255":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-39","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-an-oj","content":"The system compiles and runs student programs, then feeds the pre-provided input data to the programs and checks their output."},"256":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-40","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-an-oj","content":"If a student's output is exactly identical to the teacher-provided output, character by character, the program is considered correct; otherwise it is considered wrong."},"257":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-41","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-an-oj","content":"If memory/time limits are exceeded during execution, the program is interrupted and marked incorrect."},"258":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-42","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-an-oj","content":"After understanding the above, students should realize that if a problem does not require prompts like \"Please Input Two Number\", printing such text yourself will make your output differ from expected output, causing Wrong Answer.If a problem requires a blank line between every two output lines and you omit it, that is a format error, and vice versa.You may feel the system is bad for not auto-detecting this; in fact, this is exactly how it effectively trains programming precision and good coding habits. Many strong programmers started by complaining about this system and learned to code carefully and rigorously.To run all submissions in a unified way, the system must constrain submission format for everyone.For C/C++ learners, every submission must contain exactly one main function, it must return int, and preferably return 0, because non-zero return values are considered runtime errors by the operating system.When a compile error occurs, click the \"Compile Error\" text link for detailed explanation."},"259":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-43","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#error-err_stream_premature_close-premature-close-when-installing-in-arch-linux-development-mode","content":"Delete .yarnrc.yml and .yarn, then try again."},"260":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-44","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#why-cant-i-access-the-site-after-installation","content":"If you are using providers such as Alibaba Cloud/Tencent Cloud, ensure ports 80 and 443 are allowed in the security group."},"261":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-45","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#why-cant-i-log-in-after-configuring-reverse-proxy-caddynginx-csrftokenerror","content":"When reverse proxying, ensure the Host Header is set correctly. Details"},"262":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-46","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-back-up--restore-backup--migrate-data","content":"hydrooj backup hydrooj restore backup-xxx.zip"},"263":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-47","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-back-up--restore-backup--migrate-data","content":"After learning how crontab works, you can use sudo crontab -e to create automatic backup schedules."},"264":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-48","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#upgrade","content":"See Upgrade Guide"},"265":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-49","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-importcreate-problems","content":"There are corresponding entries on the right side of the problem list page."},"266":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-50","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-importcreate-problems","content":"Remember: do not import too many problems you do not need yet. The correct approach is to import only 5–10 required problems per training assignment. After the assignment/contest ends, let those become part of the training problemset. This keeps lower problem IDs gradually increasing in difficulty and makes self-training easier for later students. Do not chase quantity while ignoring quality. Use fewer problems you do not understand, and use them cautiously."},"267":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-51","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-restrict-access-for-unlogged-users","content":"Manage Domain -> Manage Permissions: disable the \"View this domain\" permission for Guest group."},"268":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-52","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-add-icp-filing-number-in-footer","content":"Add a line in system setting footer_extra_html: <a href=\"https://beian.miit.gov.cn/\">XX ICP XX No.</a>"},"269":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-53","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-does-time-mean-in-contestsassignments-difference-between-oi-ranking-and-normal-ranking","content":"Time means the time \"spent\" for participants to solve a problem:That is: time solved – contest start time + penalty timePenalty time = number of wrong submissions before acceptance * 20 minutes.Normal ranking is based on number of solved problems and \"spent\" time.OI ranking is based on score. Problems can be scored proportionally by pass ratio, 100 points each. If you want non-uniform score distribution, use config."},"270":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-54","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#where-does-the-script-install-oj","content":"You can get Hydro's default location with yarn global dir. (Do not modify code directly; updates will overwrite all changes there. Use the plugin API instead.)Default database files are in /data/db, but do not copy files directly; hydrooj backup is recommended.Files such as test data are stored in /data/file.Config files are in /root/.config/hydro and /root/.hydro.\nFor production servers in operation, always make an offline backup before any operation.Always unzip backup files to verify all data is included, and check backup size (large systems should have backups of hundreds of MB). If possible, verify restore success in a VM."},"271":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-55","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-the-precision-of-time-limit-and-memory-limit","content":"The literal time limit precision is 1ms, but due to OS kernel constraints, actual measured precision is usually 4ms.\nMemory limit precision is 1MB. For local native compiled languages like c/c++/pascal/freebasic/clang, it measures the program's own memory allocation; for VM/script languages, it includes memory consumed by the VM/interpreter itself."},"272":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-56","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#outdated-lockfile-please-run-yarn-install-and-try-again","content":"Then try again."},"273":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-57","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#i-want-python-to-support-numpy-and-similar-libraries-what-should-i-do","content":"If installed before 2022/8/12, run pip3 install numpy then pm2 restart hydro-sandboxOtherwise refer to the Compiler section."},"274":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-58","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#i-forgot-mongodb-accountpassword-after-using-installation-script-what-should-i-do","content":"Check /root/.hydro/config.json."},"275":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-59","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-disableenable-user-registration","content":"Registration is controlled by Guest user (uid = 0) permission PRIV_REGISTER_USER, enabled by default.\nUse hydrooj cli user setPriv 0 0 to disable registration.\nTo re-enable, use hydrooj cli user setPriv 0 8."},"276":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-60","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-disableenable-user-registration","content":"After changing it, restart hydrooj service: pm2 restart hydrooj"},"277":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-61","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#what-is-user-hydro-for-whats-the-password-can-it-log-in","content":"User Hydro (uid = 1) is only for sending system messages (similar to 10000 in QQ) and cannot log in."},"278":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-62","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-modify-website-icon","content":"Use hydrooj addon create to create a plugin, which will create /root/addon automatically.Go to /root/addon/public, and place your site icons there.You need these files in that directory (for different browsers):"},"279":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-63","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-modify-website-icon","content":"favicon-16x16.png"},"280":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-64","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-modify-website-icon","content":"favicon-32x32.png"},"281":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ-65","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ#how-to-modify-website-icon","content":"favicon-96x96.png"},"2