evelop plugins and upload them to the server (we also recommend this, because editor code completion can greatly simplify the development process). You can do the following:"},"532":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-40","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#optional-write-plugins-on-local-machine","content":"Install NodeJS and yarn on your local machine."},"533":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-41","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#optional-write-plugins-on-local-machine","content":"Follow Step 1 and use yarn init to create a project."},"534":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-42","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#optional-write-plugins-on-local-machine","content":"Open the plugin folder with VSCode."},"535":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-43","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#optional-write-plugins-on-local-machine","content":"Run yarn add hydrooj -D to install related development components."},"536":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-44","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#optional-write-plugins-on-local-machine","content":"Develop the plugin by following the instructions below."},"537":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-45","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#optional-write-plugins-on-local-machine","content":"Upload the local folder to the server and enable the uploaded plugin with hydrooj addon add <absolute plugin path>."},"538":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-46","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"Analysis: the pastebin component needs the following features:"},"539":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-47","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"Interact with the database to store/retrieve corresponding documents."},"540":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-48","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"Provide the /paste/create route to create new documents."},"541":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-49","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"Provide /paste/show/:ID to view created documents."},"542":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-50","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"Authenticate by user ID, and allow documents to be set as private to prevent others from viewing."},"543":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-51","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"In routes, all defined functions should be asynchronous. Supported functions are: prepare, get, post, post[Operation], cleanupThe process is as follows:"},"544":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-52","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"If this.response.template specifies a template, it will be rendered; otherwise, the content in this.response.body is returned directly."},"545":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-53","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"Use underscores for the operation field in form submission, and camelCase for function names."},"546":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-54","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"For example, <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"operation\" value=\"confirm_delete\"> corresponds to the postConfirmDelete function."},"547":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-55","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step2-prepare-to-write-components","content":"You should provide an apply function and mount it together with defined Handlers at global.Hydro.handler[module name].\nThe apply function will be called during initialization."},"548":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-56","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step4-template","content":"Templates use nunjucks syntax and should be placed in the templates/ folder.At the end of the request, the template is selected based on response.template, rendered with response.body, and written into response.body.If response.template is empty or request.headers['accept'] == 'application/json', the rendering step is skipped."},"549":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-57","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step5-locale","content":"Used to provide multilingual translations. The format is the same as Hydro's locale folder format."},"550":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript-58","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/dev/typescript#step6-frontend","content":"Write frontend code in the frontend folder. Files named [a-zA-Z0-9_]+.page.tsx? are automatically loaded as entry points.The paste feature does not require any additional JS-driven frontend interaction, so a minimal format example is provided below."},"551":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","type":"page","content":"Compilers and Languages","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Hydro","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler"},"552":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-0","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#language-specific-time-limit-modifications","content":"Language-specific Time Limit Modifications"},"553":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-1","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#colored-cc-compilation-error-output","content":"Colored C/C++ Compilation Error Output"},"554":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-2","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#advanced-environment-configuration","content":"Advanced Environment Configuration"},"555":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-3","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#others","content":"Others"},"556":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-4","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"Starting from 2022/8/12, to prevent host-environment changes from affecting judging consistency, Hydro uses nix by default to manage environments for instances installed after this date.If your Hydro instance was installed prior to this date, please install compilers via apt, restart the sandbox with pm2 restart hydro-sandbox, and skip this section."},"557":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-5","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"Below is a brief guide to nix operations:"},"558":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-6","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"Use nix-env -iA nixpkgs.<compiler_name> to install a new compiler, then restart the sandbox with pm2 restart hydro-sandbox for it to take effect."},"559":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-7","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"You can search for required compilers at Nixos Search.Here are examples of commonly used compilers:"},"560":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-8","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"Use nix-env -q to view the list of installed packages, and use nix-env -e <compiler_name> to remove a specific compiler.Please be careful not to accidentally delete Hydro base components. After completing your operations, you must restart the sandbox with pm2 restart hydro-sandbox for the changes to take effect."},"561":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-9","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"Some languages (specifically Java, etc.), due to their language characteristics, require a longer CPU time for compilation. This is particularly noticeable on single-core machines, where compiling even A+B might take several seconds or even tens of seconds.The expected performance can be tested by manually running the compilation command on the host:"},"562":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-10","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"At the same time, some compilers will attempt to create a large number of processes to utilize multi-core parallel compilation whenever possible. Please ensure the processLimit item in the judge settings is large enough; otherwise, compilation will fail because the compiler cannot create processes."},"563":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-11","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"When the compiler utilizes multi-core parallel compilation, Hydro sums the CPU usage of these processes as the CPU resource limit. If a compilation timeout error occurs, please adjust the compile_time_limit item (in ms) under the corresponding language option in the system settings."},"564":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-12","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"Similarly, if a memory limit exceeded error occurs, you can modify the compile_memory_limit item (in MB) for the corresponding language."},"565":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-13","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","content":"After installing a python package using sh nix-env -iA nixpkgs.python3Packages.xxxxx, if dependencies cannot be found in the sandbox environment, please refer to the Import Python packages into sandbox tutorial to update environment variables."},"566":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-14","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#language-specific-time-limit-modifications","content":"By default, the system provides double the time limit for Java and Kotlin. This behavior can be modified in the language settings:"},"567":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-15","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#colored-cc-compilation-error-output","content":"Ensure you have installed a compiler that supports colored output;"},"568":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-16","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#colored-cc-compilation-error-output","content":"In system settings, append -fdiagnostics-color=always to the C/C++ compilation commands."},"569":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-17","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#colored-cc-compilation-error-output","content":"Example:"},"570":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-18","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#advanced-environment-configuration","content":"If you require a more complex compilation environment configuration, we recommend writing a separate nix file."},"571":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-19","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#advanced-environment-configuration","content":"Copy the file above, save it as default.nix, and use nix-build to build it.After building, a result folder will be generated. Remember the path where this folder is located.Open ~/.hydro/mount.yaml and replace /root/.nix-profile in it with the compiled result folder (switching to the new environment).Then save and restart the sandbox."},"572":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-20","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#advanced-environment-configuration","content":"If you need to change the environment configuration later, simply modify the default.nix file, use nix-build to rebuild, and restart the sandbox for it to take effect.Cache files generated during the build process can be cleaned up using nix-collect-garbage."},"573":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-21","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#advanced-environment-configuration","content":"For a more detailed introduction to the nix language, please refer to the Nix Guide and Nix Manual."},"574":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler-22","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/compiler#others","content":"Recommended reading: the HydroJudge section, to learn more detailed information about judge machine settings."},"575":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","type":"page","content":"Deploy Hydro","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Hydro","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install"},"576":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-0","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Selecting a Server"},"577":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-1","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"Deploy"},"578":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-2","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","content":"Multiple deployment options are available to help you build your site. Choose the one that best fits your needs.\nIf you encounter any issues during setup, feel free to contact us."},"579":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-3","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Performance varies by provider; the specifications below are for reference only."},"580":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-4","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Minimum Requirements: 1 CPU core, 2GB RAM. (Supports ~100 concurrent users)."},"581":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-5","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Important: Avoid burstable (e.g., AWS t-series) or shared-core instances where possible, as they can cause inconsistent and inaccurate judging time measurements."},"582":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-6","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Operating System Notes:"},"583":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-7","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"CentOS 8 reached End-of-Life (EOL) on 2021-12-31 and no longer receives security patches. We recommend reinstalling your server with a supported OS."},"584":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-8","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Recommended OS: Debian 12, Debian 11, or Ubuntu 22.04. These distributions offer the best support, documentation, and success rate for beginners."},"585":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-9","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Unsupported OS: CentOS and its derivatives (Alibaba Cloud Linux, TencentOS, OpenCloudOS, etc.) are not supported."},"586":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-10","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Low-Memory Servers (≤ 2GB RAM): Avoid Ubuntu 22.04 due to its higher memory footprint. Debian 12 or 11 is recommended.\nFor experienced Linux users, Alpine Linux is an excellent choice, consuming only ~100MB RAM after boot."},"587":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-11","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Using these referral links helps support the project through small cashbacks (at no extra cost to you):"},"588":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-12","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Tencent Cloud"},"589":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-13","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Alibaba Cloud (15% discount)"},"590":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-14","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"type: warn"},"591":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-15","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Mainland China Users: Without an ICP filing, some providers (like China Telecom Cloud) block ports 80 and 443. Ensure you understand the regulations before purchasing."},"592":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-16","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"type: warn"},"593":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-17","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Virtual Machine (VM) Users:"},"594":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-18","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Hydro's database relies on the CPU AVX instruction set for optimal performance. Most virtualization software (VMware, VirtualBox, etc.) disables AVX by default; check your documentation to enable it."},"595":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-19","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Lack of exclusive CPU access can lead to inconsistent judging times."},"596":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-20","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Sudden power loss can easily corrupt VM databases. Regular backups are essential."},"597":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-21","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Docker Users:"},"598":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-22","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"When using the installation script, set the USER environment variable to root."},"599":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-23","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"You must start the container with --privileged for the judge sandbox to function."},"600":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-24","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"The development team does not provide free technical support for Docker-based deployments."},"601":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-25","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Control Panel Users (e.g., BT/BaoTa):"},"602":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-26","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"These panels often have critical security vulnerabilities. We strongly advise against using them in production."},"603":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-27","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Developers are not responsible for issues arising from panel usage."},"604":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-28","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"Free technical support is not available for deployments using third-party panels."},"605":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-29","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#selecting-a-server","content":"For paid technical support, please contact us via WeCom."},"606":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-30","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"Required Ports: Ensure ports 80, 443, 2019, 8888, 5050, 27017 are open in your firewall.\nPermissions: All installation and post-installation steps must be performed with root privileges (sudo -i)."},"607":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-31","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"Run the following command to start the installation (copy and paste to avoid errors):"},"608":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-32","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"The installation script supports advanced flags for custom requirements:"},"609":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-33","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"--no-caddy: Skips reverse proxy setup; the service will listen only on 127.0.0.1:8888."},"610":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-34","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"--judge: Installs only the standalone judge component.\nExample: . <(curl https://hydro.ac/setup.sh) --no-caddy"},"611":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-35","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"Post-Installation Tips:"},"612":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-36","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"If you are on a cloud provider (AWS, Alibaba, etc.), ensure your \"Security Group\" allows traffic on port 80."},"613":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-37","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"Open http://your-server-ip/ in your browser and register an account."},"614":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-38","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"To promote the first registered user to Super Admin, run:"},"615":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-39","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"After logging in, access the Control Panel from the navigation bar."},"616":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-40","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"Critical: In System Settings, verify the Server BaseURL. It must be the full URL (including https:// if applicable) and must end with a trailing slash / (e.g., https://hydro.ac/)."},"617":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-41","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"Loading Problems:\nYou can find a free starter problem set at hydro.ac/d/tk/p. Batch import is supported."},"618":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install-42","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install#deploy","content":"If your server is in a private network, you may need to configure \"Port Forwarding\" or a VPN for external access."},"619":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","type":"page","content":"Reverse Proxy / SSL Configuration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Hydro","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy"},"620":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy-0","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy#instances-installed-via-script-after-20221027-are-already-configured-with-caddy-reverse-proxy-automatically-please-edit-the-config-file-located-at-hydrocaddyfile-directly","content":"Instances installed via script after 2022/10/27 are already configured with Caddy reverse proxy automatically. Please edit the config file located at ~/.hydro/Caddyfile directly!"},"621":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy-1","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy#instances-installed-via-script-after-20221027-are-already-configured-with-caddy-reverse-proxy-automatically-please-edit-the-config-file-located-at-hydrocaddyfile-directly","content":"type: warn"},"622":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy-2","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy#instances-installed-via-script-after-20221027-are-already-configured-with-caddy-reverse-proxy-automatically-please-edit-the-config-file-located-at-hydrocaddyfile-directly","content":"If you use a reverse proxy, please note that the server.xff and server.xhost settings in the system settings need to be filled in correctly (in lowercase), corresponding to the header names added by the reverse proxy (usually x-forwarded-for and x-forwarded-host; some reverse proxy tools use x-real-ip instead of x-forwarded-for).Incorrect configuration of the server.xhost setting will cause issues such as users being unable to log in. (CsrfTokenError)Incorrect configuration of the server.xff setting will result in the inability to record user IPs."},"623":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy-3","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy#instances-installed-via-script-after-20221027-are-already-configured-with-caddy-reverse-proxy-automatically-please-edit-the-config-file-located-at-hydrocaddyfile-directly","content":"Except for the one-click installation script which automatically configures these settings after installing Caddy, for other tools please configure the system settings before using the tool! Otherwise, it will cause problems like users being unable to log in and user IPs not being recorded."},"624":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy-4","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy#instances-installed-via-script-after-20221027-are-already-configured-with-caddy-reverse-proxy-automatically-please-edit-the-config-file-located-at-hydrocaddyfile-directly","content":"If you use Nginx, please remember to configure the reverse proxy for the WebSocket protocol; otherwise, it will cause issues such as the judging status not refreshing automatically and the online IDE not functioning properly."},"625":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy-5","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy#instances-installed-via-script-after-20221027-are-already-configured-with-caddy-reverse-proxy-automatically-please-edit-the-config-file-located-at-hydrocaddyfile-directly","content":"Hydro supports using tools like Caddy and HAProxy for reverse proxying. Some configuration examples are provided here."},"626":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy-6","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/proxy#instances-installed-via-script-after-20221027-are-already-configured-with-caddy-reverse-proxy-automatically-please-edit-the-config-file-located-at-hydrocaddyfile-directly","content":"Hydro recommends that you use Caddy. Below is a sample Caddyfile.\nTip: If your server is located in mainland China, you need to complete ICP filing before you can use ports 80 and 443."},"627":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv","type":"page","content":"Installation on RISC-V Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Hydro","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv"},"628":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv-0","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv#system-environment","content":"System Environment"},"629":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv-1","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv#initialize-the-nix-environment","content":"Initialize the Nix Environment"},"630":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv-2","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv#build-mongodb","content":"Build MongoDB"},"631":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/install/riscv-3","page_id":"/en/d