s","content":"In the \"Manage Domain\" tab, click \"Initialize Discussion Nodes\" to set up the default forum structure for your domain."},"1150":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-19","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"In Hydro v5, access is managed through two primary roles:"},"1151":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-20","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Guest: The default role for non-logged-in users or users who have not yet joined the domain."},"1152":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-21","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Default: The standard role for members who have joined the domain."},"1153":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-22","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Key Features:"},"1154":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-23","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Self-Service Joining: Admins can enable \"Allow users to join domain\" in the domain settings."},"1155":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-24","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Rankings: Only users who have joined the domain will appear on its ranking list."},"1156":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-25","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Manual Assignment: If an admin manually assigns a role other than guest or default to a user, that user will automatically join the domain with the assigned role."},"1157":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-26","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Blocking: Explicitly setting a user's role to guest prevents them from re-joining via self-service."},"1158":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-27","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Leaving: Users can leave a domain voluntarily (unless it is the system domain) or be removed by an admin, which resets their role to guest."},"1159":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-28","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"v4 to v5 Migration:\nDuring the upgrade, Hydro automatically:"},"1160":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-29","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Marks all existing users in a domain as \"joined.\""},"1161":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-30","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v5-and-later","content":"Enables self-service joining (assigning the default role) for domains that previously had no join conditions."},"1162":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-31","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#hydro-v4","content":"In v4, non-logged-in users are guest and logged-in users are default by default. Setting a user's role to default is equivalent to removing them from the domain's specific member list."},"1163":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-32","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-contests-and-homework","content":"To create a contest or homework assignment:"},"1164":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-33","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-contests-and-homework","content":"Navigate to the \"Contest\" or \"Homework\" tab."},"1165":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-34","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-contests-and-homework","content":"Click \"Create\" on the right sidebar."},"1166":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-35","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-contests-and-homework","content":"Use the search/filter feature to add problems by ID or title."},"1167":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-36","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-contests-and-homework","content":"If a contest or homework becomes inaccessible (e.g., due to deleted problems), you can force-access the edit page by appending /edit to the URL (e.g., /contest/<id>/edit)."},"1168":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-37","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"Training plans allow you to group problems into structured paths. To create one:"},"1169":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-38","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"In the \"Training\" tab, click \"Create Training Plan\"."},"1170":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-39","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"Fill in the Title, Summary, and Description."},"1171":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-40","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"Configure the Plan using the following JSON-like format:"},"1172":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-41","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"_id: Numeric identifier for the section."},"1173":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-42","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"title: Section name."},"1174":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-43","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"requireNids: Array of section IDs that must be completed first."},"1175":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-44","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"pids: Array of problem IDs included in this section."},"1176":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain-45","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/domain#creating-training-plans","content":"If a training plan becomes inaccessible, append /edit to the URL (e.g., /training/<id>/edit) to fix the configuration."},"1177":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","type":"page","content":"User Documentation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Hydro","User Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user"},"1178":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-0","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#problem-difficulty","content":"Problem Difficulty"},"1179":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-1","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#participate-in-contests","content":"Participate in Contests"},"1180":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-2","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#post-discussions","content":"Post Discussions"},"1181":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-3","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#claim-homework","content":"Claim Homework"},"1182":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-4","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#problem-difficulty","content":"In Hydro, problem difficulty is calculated by an algorithm based on submission count, acceptance rate, and the submission time and judging result of each submission."},"1183":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-5","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#problem-difficulty","content":"In general, the larger the value, the harder the problem."},"1184":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-6","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#problem-difficulty","content":"Difficulty for new problems may be inaccurate; it becomes more reliable after enough submissions are collected."},"1185":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-7","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#problem-difficulty","content":"Earlier submissions have a larger impact on the calculated difficulty."},"1186":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-8","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#problem-difficulty","content":"Difficulty is algorithm-based, so inaccurate results are still possible."},"1187":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-9","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#participate-in-contests","content":"You can click the \"Participate\" button on the contest details page to join.\nDuring the contest, the \"Scoreboard\" displays ranking according to contest rules.\nAfter the contest ends, you can still practice problems in the contest, but the \"Scoreboard\" will stop updating."},"1188":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-10","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#post-discussions","content":"If you want to post a discussion, please enter a discussion node first, then click \"Create a discussion\" and fill in:"},"1189":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-11","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#post-discussions","content":"Title;"},"1190":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-12","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#post-discussions","content":"Content;"},"1191":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-13","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#post-discussions","content":"Highlight: if enabled, a prominent red line appears on the left side of the post (requires \"Highlight Discussion\" permission);"},"1192":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-14","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#post-discussions","content":"Pin: whether to pin the discussion (requires \"Pin Discussion\" permission)."},"1193":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-15","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#post-discussions","content":"Then click \"Create\" to publish."},"1194":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user-16","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user#claim-homework","content":"On the homework details page, you can click \"Claim Homework\".Before homework starts, you cannot view the problems in it.During the homework period, your progress and others' progress are counted in real time on the \"Scoreboard\".After homework enters the extension period, you can still submit, but scoreboard scores are converted by percentage according to extension penalty rules.After the homework deadline, you can still practice problems, but the \"Scoreboard\" will stop updating."},"1195":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","type":"page","content":"Permission System","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Hydro","User Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission"},"1196":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-0","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#privilege","content":"Privilege"},"1197":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-1","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#permission","content":"Permission"},"1198":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-2","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#roles","content":"Roles"},"1199":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-3","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#join-domain","content":"Join Domain"},"1200":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-4","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#hydro-v5","content":"Hydro v5"},"1201":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-5","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#hydro-v4","content":"Hydro v4"},"1202":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-6","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","content":"Hydro's permission system uses a two-layer structure: Privilege (PRIV) and Permission (PERM).Permissions are represented internally with bit operations. Definitions and values can be found in the source code."},"1203":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-7","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#privilege","content":"Privilege refers to permissions a user has across the whole system, effective in all Domains, such as creating users, editing system settings, creating Domains, viewing Domains, etc."},"1204":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-8","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#privilege","content":"Specifically, PRIV.PRIV_USER_PROFILE controls whether an account can log in as a normal account. Without this privilege, the account cannot log in (banned)."},"1205":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-9","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#privilege","content":"Common needs:"},"1206":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-10","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#privilege","content":"If you do not want regular users to upload files, disable PRIV_CREATE_FILE for the default role"},"1207":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-11","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#privilege","content":"If you need to disable site messages, disable PRIV_SEND_MESSAGE"},"1208":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-12","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#permission","content":"Permission refers to permissions a user has within a single Domain, such as creating problems/contests, posting/deleting discussions, etc."},"1209":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-13","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#permission","content":"If PERM.PERM_VIEW is disabled, that user cannot view this Domain."},"1210":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-14","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#roles","content":"Usually we need to assign the same permissions to a specific group of users. With many users, this becomes chaotic and hard to manage, so we designed roles for batch operations and management.Roles are for Domain-level permissions (PERM). Three built-in roles are provided:"},"1211":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-15","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#roles","content":"guest (applies to non-logged-in users, including banned users)"},"1212":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-16","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#roles","content":"default (applies to all users without an assigned role, including users not joined to the Domain)"},"1213":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-17","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#roles","content":"root (has all permissions)"},"1214":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-18","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#roles","content":"Normally, if you need special Domain permission control, you should create a new role (for example, member) and assign selected users to it.Removing a role assignment from a user in a Domain is equivalent to setting that user's role to default.If needed, you can also create other roles such as teacher or admin.Because there may be many users in the system (tens of thousands or even hundreds of thousands), only users whose role is not default are shown in the user list."},"1215":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-19","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#hydro-v5","content":"See the explanation in the Domain section."},"1216":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission-20","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/permission#hydro-v4","content":"The process of joining a Domain is essentially the process where a user self-serves their own role from default to another role (such as member) through some method.So choosing guest or default as the role in a join-domain invitation link is meaningless."},"1217":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"page","content":"Notes on Creating Common Hydro Problem Types","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create"},"1218":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-0","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#0-hydro-problem-storage-format","content":"0. Hydro problem storage format"},"1219":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-1","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#1-create-the-simplest-oj-problem","content":"1. Create the simplest OJ problem"},"1220":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-2","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#2-function-interactive-problems","content":"2. Function-interactive problems"},"1221":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-3","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#3-semi-checker-mode--custom-checker-and-modified-output-handling","content":"3. Semi-checker mode — custom checker and modified output handling"},"1222":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-4","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#4-fully-automatic-checker-problems","content":"4. Fully automatic checker problems"},"1223":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-5","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#5-file-io-based-tests","content":"5. File I/O based tests"},"1224":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-6","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#6-subtask-testing","content":"6. Subtask testing"},"1225":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-7","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#7-objective-problem-creation","content":"7. Objective problem creation"},"1226":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-8","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#8-summary","content":"8. Summary"},"1227":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-9","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"Author: laomaiqq: 29985091Website: http://82.157.98.222:8888/Date: 2022/03/16"},"1228":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-10","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"This article records the author's practical experiments while using Hydro, and I hope it helps everyone. It includes the following content:"},"1229":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-11","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"Hydro problem storage format"},"1230":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-12","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"Creating the simplest OJ problem"},"1231":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-13","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"OJ problems with custom header files (function-interactive problems)"},"1232":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-14","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"Semi-automatic checker problems (no need to input expected output manually)"},"1233":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-15","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"Fully checker-based problems (no need to input input/output data manually)"},"1234":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-16","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"Specifying input and output files"},"1235":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-17","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"Multiple subtasks"},"1236":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-18","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","content":"Objective problems (fill-in-the-blank and multiple-choice with standard answers)"},"1237":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-19","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#0-hydro-problem-storage-format","content":"If you want to prepare problems locally and then upload them in batches, the format below should help.Each problem should use its own directory, with the directory name as the problem number such as 1, 2, 3, 4, etc.Each problem directory usually contains the following:problem_zh.md This file is the problem content, i.e., problem statement, in markdown format.problem.yaml file. This is the problem configuration information, such as title and tags.testdata subdirectory, corresponding to files in the test data section on the website.It must contain at least one config.yaml file to describe judge type; see examples below for details.If a problem has test cases, each case should provide at least one .in file and one output file (some test types do not require this; see details below).additional_file subdirectory stores extra files for contestants, such as header files, images, PDF documents, etc. In the problem markdown document, you can provide download links like this: [text](file://xxx.txt)"},"1238":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-20","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#0-hydro-problem-storage-format","content":"Below are the manual steps for entering various problem types, i.e., operations after logging in and clicking create problem, as shown below:"},"1239":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-21","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#0-hydro-problem-storage-format","content":"Assume all problem statements use the markdown document below:"},"1240":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-22","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#1-create-the-simplest-oj-problem","content":"Problem URL: http://82.157.98.222:8888/p/P10000"},"1241":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-23","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#1-create-the-simplest-oj-problem","content":"After creating a new problem, edit the statement content, enter problem ID and title, then click Create, as shown below."},"1242":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-24","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#1-create-the-simplest-oj-problem","content":"You will then see the interface below. Click Create File, with filename 1.in, representing input for case 1."},"1243":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-25","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#1-create-the-simplest-oj-problem","content":"Edit 1.in content as two integers, e.g., 2 and 3, separated by space, as shown below, then click Confirm."},"1244":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-26","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#1-create-the-simplest-oj-problem","content":"Similarly create a 1.out file with content 5. Note the numeric index must match the .in file. The created file list should look like this."},"1245":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-27","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#1-create-the-simplest-oj-problem","content":"Now input and expected output for the first case are ready, and the problem can be solved."},"1246":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-28","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#1-create-the-simplest-oj-problem","content":"AC code for this problem:"},"1247":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-29","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#2-function-interactive-problems","content":"Problem URL: http://82.157.98.222:8888/p/P10001The difference from type 1 is that the problem setter provides an extra header file to contestants. Contestants can include this header in their main function to call provided functions, or implement functions declared in the header."},"1248":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-30","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#2-function-interactive-problems","content":"Statement input and test data input are the same as type 1."},"1249":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-31","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#2-function-interactive-problems","content":"This problem additionally uploads two files: tools.h and config.yaml, as shown below."},"1250":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-32","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create#2-function-interactive-problems","content":"tools.h content:"},"1251":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create-33","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/user/problem-create","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/do